---
scope: "The standing rule that UART transport is BASELINE firmware in every ComposeIO board env — not a per-board feature. Specifies the rule and its shape-based exemption, the measured cost of the transport, the RAM/flash floor below which a waiver may be granted, what a waived board loses and must provide instead, and the build-time assertion that makes the rule enforceable rather than remembered. Written 2026-08-13 as workstream B of the fleet-baseline plan, after an audit found the rule already satisfied by accident in all eleven firmware envs."
audience: "ComposeIO/ComposeUX architects, firmware developers adding a board env, and whoever selects silicon for a new node"
boundary: "IN: the compile-in policy, the audit verdict per env, the waiver floor and its arithmetic, the obligations a waiver creates, and the CMake guard. OUT: the UART transport's own design ([CXC-BOARD-HW-UART-SLAVE]), the wire frame format ([BP-UART-FRAME]), config delivery over the bus ([SPEC:CXC-CONFIG-BUS]), and per-board pin assignment."
not-this: "Not a claim that every board must USE UART at runtime — a board may select any transport; the rule is that the code is PRESENT so the wire path exists when the radio does not. Not a hardware requirement for a UART peripheral beyond two GPIOs. Not a general policy about compiling everything in: it names one file and one reason."
depends-on: [60-board-hardware-inventory.lts, 61-config-over-bus.lts, 31-composeux-board-bringup.lts]
domain: plt.cux
confidentiality: internal-only
artifact-readiness: concept-capture
